// Regression test for the "Missing annotation" internal error: a
// driver whose LHS component exists but whose declared type failed to
// resolve must not cascade into a spurious "Missing annotation" on
// the RHS.
//
// `Instruction` is undefined, so `wire instruction` is diagnosed
// `Unresolved type Instruction` and the component analysis records the
// component with no type.  The driver `it := #Lda` then has no expected
// type, so `#Lda` is left unannotated.  The `skip_validate` guard in
// `build_typing` (virdant/src/types/typing.rs) must recognize this case
// (LHS resolves, but its type is unresolved) alongside the already-
// handled case of an LHS path that does not resolve at all, and skip
// the validate pass instead of flagging every unannotated node.

pub mod Test {
    wire instruction : Instruction {
        // CHECK: Unresolved type Instruction
        // CHECK-NOT: Missing annotation
        it := #Lda
    }
}

// CHECK: Check failed
